From 48069f4d64d956d26d9c86f6ddef5bf050824dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:31:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Layout: scale only the nav rail and control bar; drop
 the status bar

The Scale setting (now "Bar Scale") used to multiply every font, icon and
stylesheet size, so raising it blew up page content that already fits the
screen. Page content now always draws at 1x; the setting only sizes the nav
rail and the control bar (its quick views and plugins' status icons
included), which get their own copy of the stylesheet at that scale.

The top status bar (a clock) is removed along with its setting: the
TrailCommand plugin shows the date and time in the control bar.
